# ESP32 Home Automation System

This project demonstrates a WiFi-based Home Automation System using the ESP32 microcontroller. It allows users to control home appliances remotely over a WiFi network.

## Project Overview

The project was developed to understand IoT-based home automation using the ESP32. It focuses on wireless device control and embedded system implementation.

## Features

- WiFi-based appliance control
- ESP32 microcontroller
- Relay control for electrical devices
- IoT-based remote operation
- Embedded C programming

## Technologies Used

- ESP32
- Arduino IDE
- Embedded C
- WiFi Communication
- Relay Module

## Project Files

This folder contains:

- Source Code
- Project Report
- Circuit Diagram included in the report
- Components List

## Learning Outcomes

- ESP32 programming
- IoT fundamentals
- WiFi communication
- Relay interfacing
- Embedded system development

This project was developed as part of my Electronics and Communication Engineering (ECE) learning and is intended for educational and internship portfolio purposes.